# Architecture (IronSight)

- Prefer readable, straightforward code and small cohesive functions.
- Reuse existing patterns before introducing new abstractions.
- Keep UI, domain/business logic, and data/infrastructure concerns separated.
- Depend on interfaces at architectural boundaries.
- Keep vendor SDKs and persistence details out of domain and presentation layers.
- Avoid unnecessary packages, speculative abstractions, architecture rewrites, premature optimization, and duplicated business rules.
- Validate at trust boundaries; fail clearly; preserve recoverable user data.
- Design external-service failures to degrade gracefully when the product can continue safely.
- Do not remove existing functionality without permission.
- Stop and ask before major refactors, architecture changes, or new dependencies.
